# Hand-authored architecture map -> d2 -> svg via `sh`.
#
# Proof-of-capability: the sprefa v4 architecture graph is supplied as
# hand-made facts (no resolver needed yet). sprf maintains them, projects
# to styled d2 source (containers + classes + shapes), writes the .d2,
# and shells out to `d2` to render the svg.
#
# Run from repo root:
#   cargo run --manifest-path v4/Cargo.toml --bin sprefa-run -- \
#     v4/examples/arch-d2-map.sprf --root . --show-rows
#
# Parser workarounds kept intentionally:
#   - render.markdown body's first non-space token is literal text
#     (a d2 vars/title header), never `${`.
#   - no `"` adjacent to `${`, and no `#` color literals (would need
#     escaping near `${`); use d2 named colors instead.
#   - node ids carry an `n_` literal prefix; tiers an `arch.tN` path.
#   - label/edge text strips `;()/|` so split+regex stay clean.

rule(:arch_node, ID?, GROUP?, KLASS?, LABEL?, ALLOC?);
rule(:arch_edge, SRC?, DST?, REL?);
rule(:arch_group, GID?, GLABEL?);

# --- processing strata: tier id | display label ---
# Ordered top-to-bottom by when the .sprf is first touched.
`t1|1 · parse · first read of the sprf
t2|2 · lower · CST to rules
t3|3 · rule · the lowered unit
t4|4 · op registry · resolved during lower
t5|5 · runtime traits · the op contract
t6|6 · execute · run the op chain
t7|7 · facts · derived rows land
t8|8 · reactive state · subscribe and keep-alive
t9|9 · rule-call dispatch · drives expand`
  > split`
`
  > re`(?P<GID>[^|]+)\|(?P<GLABEL>.+)`
  > arch_group(GID, GLABEL);

# --- node facts: id | group | class | label ---
# class drives the d2 visual tier (see classes block in projection).
# 5th field is the Rust value/alloc the node owns, surfaced as a
# hover tooltip (d2 has no <details>; node tooltip is the
# hidden-until-hover equivalent that survives a static svg export --
# connection tooltips do NOT). No ; { } | in alloc text.
`host_parse|t1|stage|host_parse. tree-sitter CST per host file|&tree_sitter::Tree over host file bytes
walk_program|t2|stage|walk_program. CST to FusedRule list|Vec<PipeAst> lowered to FusedRule
FusedRule|t3|data|FusedRule. one lowered rule plus its op chain|FusedRule struct, kind plus fused_sql
OpRegistry|t4|reg|OpRegistry. name to OperatorDef table|HashMap<str, Arc<dyn OperatorDef>>
split_op|t4|op|split. backtick literal to row stream|Arc<dyn OperatorDef> SplitDef
re_op|t4|op|re. regex capture groups to named terms|Arc<dyn OperatorDef> ReDef regex::Regex
render_op|t4|op|render.markdown. template body to text|Arc<dyn OperatorDef> RenderDef
sh_op|t4|op|sh. shell out effect node|Arc<dyn OperatorDef> wraps std::process::Command
OperatorDef|t5|trait|OperatorDef. compile-time op trait. lower bridge|trait, fn lower -> Box<dyn Component>
Component|t5|trait|Component. runtime op trait. render render_batch|Box<dyn Component>, render_batch over a tick
Node|t5|trait|Node. output algebra. Emit Many Park Done|enum Node, Emit Many Park Done
RenderCtx|t5|trait|RenderCtx. pipe hash depth generation bus|&RenderCtx, pipe_hash depth tick bus
Cursor|t5|data|Cursor. payload. focal term plus named terms|Arc<Cursor> with Vec<CursorTerm>
expand|t6|stage|expand. run op chain bind term cursors|PipeInstance over Vec<Arc<Cursor>> batches
FactStore|t7|store|FactStore. derived rows keyed by rule name|rule_facts rows, blake3 _id keys
FactRuntimeGraph|t8|store|FactRuntimeGraph. subscribe support dirty sweep|Z-set deltas plus subscribe and support edges
RuntimeGraph|t8|store|RuntimeGraph. v4 facade over FactRuntimeGraph|thin facade over FactRuntimeGraph
owner_uri|t8|data|owner_uri. owner identity key. switchMap key|OwnerUri, the switchMap key
Subscribe|t8|data|Subscribe. source in-edge. owner consumes source|subscribe_edge, a source stream in-edge
support|t8|data|support. keyed-children keep-alive set|support_edge refcount keep-alive set
call_r|t9|dispatch|CALL r. eager rule-call. emit rows now|eager expand, emit rows now
force_r|t9|dispatch|force r. drain rule to fixpoint|loop expand until no delta
query_r|t9|dispatch|QUERY r. subscribe to rule rows|read rule_facts, body never runs`
  > split`
`
  > re`(?P<ID>[^|]+)\|(?P<GROUP>[^|]+)\|(?P<KLASS>[^|]+)\|(?P<LABEL>[^|]+)\|(?P<ALLOC>.+)`
  > arch_node(ID, GROUP, KLASS, LABEL, ALLOC);

# --- edge facts: src | dst | relation ---
`host_parse|walk_program|CST feeds walk
walk_program|FusedRule|lowers each rule
FusedRule|expand|op chain executed by
expand|FactStore|emits derived rows
expand|OpRegistry|resolves op by name
OpRegistry|split_op|registers
OpRegistry|re_op|registers
OpRegistry|render_op|registers
OpRegistry|sh_op|registers
split_op|OperatorDef|implements
re_op|OperatorDef|implements
render_op|OperatorDef|implements
sh_op|OperatorDef|implements
OperatorDef|Component|lower compiles to
Component|Node|dispatch returns
Component|RenderCtx|dispatch reads
Cursor|Component|batch input to
expand|Cursor|binds term cursors
FactStore|FactRuntimeGraph|rows land in
RuntimeGraph|FactRuntimeGraph|delegates all state
Subscribe|FactRuntimeGraph|inserts subscribe edge
owner_uri|RuntimeGraph|keys owner instances
support|FactRuntimeGraph|refcount keep-alive
FactRuntimeGraph|Node|dirty sweep re-runs owners
call_r|expand|triggers eager expand
force_r|expand|drains to fixpoint
query_r|FactRuntimeGraph|subscribes via`
  > split`
`
  > re`(?P<SRC>[^|]+)\|(?P<DST>[^|]+)\|(?P<REL>.+)`
  > arch_edge(SRC, DST, REL);

# --- project facts -> styled d2 source, write, then render via sh ---
# NOTE: the body opens with a literal d2 vars/title header so the first
# non-space token is NOT `${` (parser workaround). A root `arch` grid
# container (grid-rows: 9, grid-columns: 1) stacks the tiers top-to-bottom
# in code order; nodes are `arch.tN.n_ID`. Colors are d2 named colors to
# avoid `#` literals near `${`.
`arch-map`
  > render.markdown`vars: {
  d2-config: {
    layout-engine: elk
    theme-id: 300
    pad: 40
  }
}

title: sprefa v4 architecture {
  near: top-center
  shape: text
  style: { font-size: 30; bold: true }
}

direction: down

classes: {
  stage: {
    shape: rectangle
    style: { fill: royalblue; stroke: navy; font-color: white; border-radius: 8; bold: true; shadow: true }
  }
  data: {
    shape: rectangle
    style: { fill: aliceblue; stroke: steelblue; border-radius: 12; font-size: 13 }
  }
  store: {
    shape: cylinder
    style: { fill: cornsilk; stroke: darkgoldenrod; font-size: 13 }
  }
  reg: {
    shape: package
    style: { fill: lavender; stroke: indigo; font-size: 13 }
  }
  op: {
    shape: hexagon
    style: { fill: thistle; stroke: indigo; font-size: 12 }
  }
  trait: {
    shape: rectangle
    style: { fill: honeydew; stroke: seagreen; border-radius: 4; multiple: true; font-size: 13 }
  }
  dispatch: {
    shape: diamond
    style: { fill: mistyrose; stroke: firebrick; font-size: 12; bold: true }
  }
}

arch: sprf to facts processing strata {
  grid-rows: 9
  grid-columns: 1
  grid-gap: 34
  style: { fill: white; stroke: white; font-size: 13 }
}
${ arch_group?(GID?, GLABEL?)
  > render.markdown`arch.${GID}: ${GLABEL} {
  style: { fill: ghostwhite; stroke: slategray; stroke-dash: 3; font-size: 16; bold: true }
}
`
}
${ arch_node?(ID?, GROUP?, KLASS?, LABEL?, ALLOC?)
  > render.markdown`arch.${GROUP}.n_${ID}: ${LABEL} { class: ${KLASS}; tooltip: ${ALLOC} }
`
}
${ arch_edge?(SRC?, DST?, REL?)
  > arch_node?(SRC, SG?, SK?, SL?, SA?)
  > arch_node?(DST, DG?, DK?, DL?, DA?)
  > render.markdown`arch.${SG}.n_${SRC} -> arch.${DG}.n_${DST}: ${REL} { style.font-size: 11 }
`
}
`
  > write_file`v4/examples/arch-map.d2`
  > sh`d2 v4/examples/arch-map.d2 v4/examples/arch-map.svg && echo d2-rendered`;
